2. The rights as referred to in paragraph (1) include: a. accessing inclusive education at all units, paths, types, and levels of education without discrimination, with the support of inclusive facilities and infrastructure; b. obtaining decent work and livelihood in accordance with their capacity, skills, and special needs, as well as a supportive work environment; c. obtaining equal treatment to play an active role in development and enjoy the results of development fairly;
d. obtaining accessibility in various fields of life, including infrastructure, technology, transportation, public services, and information, in order to increase independence and social participation;
e. obtaining equal treatment before the law, including legal protection that is sensitive to the needs of vulnerable groups;
f. obtaining rehabilitation services, social assistance, and other support to improve welfare and social independence; and g. having equal opportunities in developing talents, abilities, and social life without structural or cultural barriers.
3. The Government, society, and the business world are obliged to play an active role in realizing equality for women with disabilities and other social inclusion groups by providing inclusive and sustainable policies, programs, and services.

7.4.text:
Article 3

1. The Implementation of Protection and Empowerment of Women is intended to realize protection for women from acts of violence, exploitation and discrimination as well as to increase the capacity and welfare of Women in various aspects of life.
2. The implementation of protection and empowerment of women aims to: a. prevent all forms of violence, exploitation, and discrimination against women;
b. provide services and recovery for victims; c. fulfill the special needs of women; and d. improve the quality of life of women.
3. The scope of this Regional Regulation includes: a. women's rights;
b. efforts to protect women;
c. empowerment of women;
d. obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government;
e. institutions;
f. coordination and cooperation;
g. participation;
h. monitoring, evaluation, and reporting;
i. awards; and j. funding.

REGENT OF KEBUMEN,

Considering:
a. that women are citizens who have human rights that must be protected, respected, maintained, and must not be ignored, reduced, or deprived by anyone, thus requiring guarantee of protection from acts of violence, exploitation, and discrimination and need to be empowered so that they can actualize their potential optimally;
b. that in society there are still many women who experience violence, discrimination, and injustice and often face major obstacles in accessing adequate education, health, and social protection services which have a negative impact on their welfare and self-development;
c. that in order to protect and provide means for self-actualization of women in society in Kebumen Regency, regulation regarding protection and empowerment of women is required;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Implementation of Protection and Empowerment of Women;

In View of:
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 13 of 1950 concerning Formation of Regency Regions within the Province of Central Java (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1950 Number 42);
3. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as has been amended several times, most recently by Law Number 6 of 2023 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 2 of 2022 concerning Job Creation into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2023 Number 41, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6856);
4. Law Number 11 of 2023 concerning Central Java Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2023 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6867);

With the Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF KEBUMEN REGENCY and

